## Terminal Command Behavior

- After running a terminal command, if output has been received and there is no further activity, treat the command as complete — do not wait indefinitely for a new prompt.
- Prefer commands that exit cleanly. Avoid interactive commands (e.g. `less`, `vim`, `top`) unless explicitly needed — use flags like `--no-pager`, `| cat`, `| head`, or `-y` to keep commands non-interactive.
- For long-running commands, prefer adding `; echo "DONE_$?"` at the end so completion is unambiguous.
- If a terminal command appears stuck on pending despite output being shown, proceed by considering the command complete.
